# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# No trailing slash, deliberately. A trailing slash matches a directory and
# NOT a symlink of the same name -- and a symlink is exactly what an agent
# working in a worktree creates to reuse the main checkout's interpreter.
# `git add -A` then commits it, and the next --ff-only merge into the main
# checkout replaces the real .venv directory with a symlink pointing at
# itself: "too many levels of symbolic links", interpreter gone. Happened.
.venv

# Test artifacts
.pytest_cache/

# A case archive. Still the exchange format the client imports and exports, and
# a real one holds an incident's whole record.
*.iccase

# Agent scratch space. Worktrees are checkouts of this same repo living
# inside it; without this a `git add -A` in the main checkout commits an
# entire second copy of the tree. Remove them when their work is merged
# (see "Worktrees: clean up after yourself" in .claude/CLAUDE.md).
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-machine Claude Code permission state, not a project setting.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/CLAUDE.local.md

# OS/editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/

*.docx
# Build-time only. Not a licence problem -- dev dependencies do not ship, and
# the runtimes are MIT, which AGPL-3.0 accepts. The cost is that a tree
# committed once cannot be taken back out of history.
node_modules/

# A generated TLS pair. **Never committed**: a private key in history cannot
# be taken back out, and this one is minted per checkout on first start.
.tls/

# Evidence artefacts a dev run attaches. Content-addressed bytes from a real
# incident are the last thing that should reach a repository going public.
.evidence/

# Left behind when Storybook cannot bind its port.
ui/debug-storybook.log

# Playwright run artefacts: traces, screenshots, the HTML report.
test-results/
playwright-report/

# The visual sweep's captures and its baseline: evidence for a person to
# read, regenerated by `npm run visual`, never reviewed as a diff.
server/.visual/
# The capability audit's report: evidence for a person to read, regenerated
# by `npm run audit:affordances`.
server/.affordance-audit/

# Bind sources for the container tier. Inside the repository on purpose: the
# dev container mounts the workspace host-path-to-same-host-path, so this is
# the one path a daemon resolving against macOS spells the same way the client
# does. Created and torn down per test.
.container-test-tmp/

# The stack's credentials, written by `docker/secrets.sh`. Never committed:
# these are the only copy, and a password in the tree is a password every
# reader of this repository holds.
.env

# **Not committed: it executes remote code on open.**
# `.mcp.json` is auto-loaded by Claude Code for anyone who opens this
# repository, and the entry `shadcn mcp init` writes runs
# `npx shadcn@latest mcp` - an unpinned package fetched and executed with no
# review. Whether every contributor runs that is the maintainer's call, not a
# default that arrives with a clone. Keep it local, or pin the version and
# commit it deliberately.
.mcp.json
